# the types, constants and global variables of a module
#
# a scalar, vector, pointer or function type is declared once by its shape,
# as spir-v allows no two of them alike. an aggregate is declared once for
# each layout it is held by: plainly, where its storage class fixes no
# layout, or with the offsets and strides the target's data layout gives it
# in a class that does, as a Uniform, PushConstant or StorageBuffer block's,
# whose variable's own type is decorated as the Block it is. a layout is
# named by its key, the class it is laid out in shifted up two, whether it is
# laid out and whether it is a block, so the layout of a member is its
# aggregate's without the block. a type that holds no aggregate has one
# layout, whatever key it is asked for by.
#
# an integer type is unsigned and its signedness is the instruction's, but
# the Sampled Type of an image of signed texels, which is signed, an i1 is a
# bool, and a union is held as its largest member, the first of those
# alike, since logical addressing reinterprets no memory. a width of an
# integer or float that core spir-v does not hold needs its capability,
# which the module then declares, and an 8- or 16-bit scalar in memory the
# host shares needs the storage capability of its width and class. where the
# build does not hold Int8 or Int16, mirl.legal.narrow carries every value of
# the width in a 32-bit one, so the width is left only in memory and in what
# moves a value to or from it: memory the host shares needs its storage
# capability alone, and a member of an aggregate or memory no host shares
# needs the width's own capability, which refuses the module without it.
#
# a block, and what a physical pointer reaches, keeps the target's own
# layout, the host's, and one that breaks the rules vulkan holds its class to
# is refused. a pointer into PhysicalStorageBuffer is made by OpBitcast,
# which the storage capabilities do not admit for an 8- or 16-bit type, so
# one behind it needs the width's own capability as well. a storage block where the
# selection has no StorageBuffer class is a Uniform one decorated BufferBlock.

